- Native RNIEP matrix witness: Section 5 says even NP membership of rational RNIEP is unknown because a realizing matrix may have real entries and exact verification is not generally polynomial. Restricting the generator to rational matrices repairs verification but leaves no paper-backed hardness result for the inverse-generated distribution.
- Theorem 5.3’s partition witness: this is exact and cheaply verifiable, but inverse generation creates a planted PARTITION distribution. The paper proves only worst-case hardness through Lemma 4.1; it gives neither distributional hardness nor a compact sub-300-operation route. A pseudo-polynomial DP/meet-in-the-middle/LLL attack is the mechanism that must be measured, not hidden behind the theorem title.

